WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.569 --> 00:00:14.128
I may look like a nice English lady in a sensible cardigan, but these days it's a thin veneer and it's starting to crack

00:00:15.369 --> 00:00:21.029
Who wants to bring kids into this bloody world? My point is I just don't think that the world needs more kids

00:00:21.029 --> 00:00:22.280
I think we get it

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:30.960
Tucker Crowe, one of the most unsung figures of alternative rock. Hasn't been seen in 20 years. That's him

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:33.320
Wow, he's so gorgeous. Thank you

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:37.320
I think I've had enough Tucker bloody Crowes to last 20 lifetimes

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:42.620
Tucker has a new album and I don't want to spend my time with someone who doesn't get it

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:51.020
Oh, somebody new. "Juliet Naked is a naked attempt to squeeze a few more quid out of a long-dead career"

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:53.860
You wrote this

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:58.880
There's the strangest thing. I met someone on the Internet. You're finally entering the modern age.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:01.540
He read that review I posted

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:05.220
"You nailed it. I couldn't have explained it better myself" -Tucker Crowe

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:08.040
Tucker Crowe? As in Duncan's idol Tucker Crowe? Yes

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:10.360
"Yeah, it's really me. What's your story?"

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:18.960
Dear Tucker, it's really odd to be saying all this to a stranger, but I have a hunch I've wasted the last 15 years of my life

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:25.180
I don't imagine this as much of a consolation, but I'm ashamed to say that two decades have slipped through my fingers

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:27.260
At least you have a past to live up to

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:31.300
Big news. I'm coming to London. Would you like to meet for a drink?

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:37.720
Beautiful spot

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:39.120
You're not downstairs, are you?

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:45.440
That's me in my high school chess club. I can explain this. I'm not trying to trap, or cut your head off or whatever

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:49.860
Hey! How've you been?

00:01:49.870 --> 00:01:55.600
Duncan Thompson. Tucker Crowe. I'm Stevie Wonder. Just take it easy. Real mature, honey

00:01:57.420 --> 00:02:02.059
What are you drinking Tucker Crowe? Glass of water. I'm not getting a famous American rock star a glass of water

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:05.960
I'm not that famous of okay, and I'm an alcoholic. Well, you'll fit right in

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:12.140
I was wondering if you'd be interested in me? Do you think there's any way back for me?

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:16.279
You sure this doesn't have something to do with your idol coming along and fancying me?

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:20.920
Please, how do we know that's even him? Well, I have a passport.  Well, that would be super

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:25.420
Well, all of this seems to be in order. Really? Oh thank god

